{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ReaPackLab\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaPackLab is a fork of ReaPack designed for managed REAPER environments.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This package provides a Developer ID-signed macOS 15.0+ Apple Silicon binary. It is the centrally managed edition, not the separate ReaPackLabSetup bootstrap extension. This release is not notarized. Use in a clean test REAPER installation before classroom deployment.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Based on ReaPack by Christian Fillion (LGPL-3.0-or-later).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ReaPackLab\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b ReaPackLab} is the release repository for the centrally managed REAPER package manager in the ReaLab project, based on ReaPack by Christian Fillion.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Current stable release: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLab/releases/tag/v0.14.3"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
v0.14.3
}}}
} \u8212- macOS 15.0 or later, Apple Silicon (ARM64). The binary embeds version {\b 0.14.3} and is Developer ID Application signed, securely timestamped, and built with hardened runtime. Other platforms are not listed in this distribution.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The separate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLabSetup"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPackLabSetup
}}}
 bootstrap companion has its own version and feed. It is not included in the main binary.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Security and verification\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Signed, not notarized.} Signing does not establish Apple notarization or Gatekeeper acceptance; macOS warnings may still occur. Do not assume that this release validates all deployment or recovery workflows. Test in an isolated REAPER resource directory before classroom or wider deployment.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each new release includes the dylib, {\f1 ReaPackLab-SHA256SUMS.txt}, and {\f1 ReaPackLab-provenance.json}, recording the final signed-byte hash and build identity. Existing releases remain unchanged. The binaries in older release tags retain their original signatures and embedded versions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Repository folder names\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 New/unowned approved repositories use their readable index names for Scripts and Effects. Existing installed registry owners, including earlier {\f1 Repository-\u8230 ?} names, are preserved; this update does not automatically rename or migrate old folders. Deleting only folders does not reset recorded ownership. Test fresh naming in a separate REAPER resource directory rather than deleting a working registry.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Mac case/Unicode namespace collisions are checked before new identities become writable, and partial discovery failures do not keep revoked subscriptions enabled. All nine native test groups passed on Mac and Linux; full live-REAPER installation/restart behavior still needs isolated testing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Repository / installation\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaPack repository index URL:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rockumk/ReaPackLab/master/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Native extension metadata is maintained in {\f1 Extensions/ReaPackLab.ext}. Its active {\f1 @provides} entry selects the verified, versioned ARM64 release asset and installs it into REAPER's {\f1 UserPlugins} directory. Restart REAPER after installing or updating native extensions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The index is generated automatically with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
reapack-index
}}}
 after verified assets and package metadata are published. Generated package entries are not edited by hand; historical versions are retained. See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "Extensions/README.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Extensions/README.md
}}}
 for packaging conventions. Documented platform examples are not a claim that those platforms have release assets.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Development and scope\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/rockumk/ReaPackLabDev"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPackLabDev
}}}
 is the development repository (access restricted). This distribution repository and its automatic source archives contain packaging metadata, not the development source tree. Public provenance records identify the exact development commit and Actions build without publishing private source or logs.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaPackLab is the managed package manager; ReaPackLabSetup is a separate bootstrap companion. Test installation and upgrades in isolated REAPER resources before using them with an existing managed installation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 License and acknowledgments\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaPackLab is derived from ReaPack by Christian Fillion. ReaPack is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or later. Derived source and binaries must retain the applicable license and attribution notices. Packaging tools and repository-format documentation are provided by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack
}}}
 ecosystem.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaPackLab is an independent project and is not affiliated with Cockos, Inc.\par}
}
